 class="tag">Big Ten · 4-1</span><p>Iowa&#x27;s unbeaten start ended against Ohio State. The Hawkeyes managed 238 total yards and 39 rushing yards in the 31-14 loss.</p><dl><dt>Latest result</dt><dd>2026-10-03 · L 14–31 home vs Ohio State</dd><dt>AP movement</dt><dd>Down 6</dd><dt>Next game</dt><dd>2026-10-10 · away vs Washington</dd></dl><details><summary>Recalibration week · analysis</summary><p>The loss exposed the challenge against a top offense and defensive front. The response matters more than the six-place slide.</p><p><strong>Watch next:</strong> Rebuild offensive traction on the road in Seattle.</p><p class="source-ref">Sources: <a href="https://ohiostatebuckeyes.com/news/2026/10/3/football-no-5-buckeyes-grab-ranked-win-over-no-14-iowa">Ohio State defeats Iowa ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.ncaa.com/news/football/article/2026-10-04/top-five-holds-alabama-rises-latest-ap-top-25-college-football-rankings">October 4 AP Top 25 table ↗</a> · <a href="https://hawkeyesports.com/news/2026/01/28/big-ten-announces-2026-football-schedule">Iowa 2026 schedule announcement ↗</a></p></details><p class="source-ref">Sources: <a href="https://www.ncaa.com/news/football/article/2026-10-04/top-five-holds-alabama-rises-latest-ap-top-25-college-football-rankings">October 4 AP Top 25 table ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.afca.com/missouri-bounces-back-with-dominant-win/">October 4 US LBM Coaches Poll ↗</a></p></article><article class="card" data-card data-group="Big Ten" data-status="Unbeaten" id="program-ucla"><span class="rank">21</span><p class="meta">AP No. 21 · Coaches No. 22</p><h3>UCLA</h3><span class="tag">Big Ten · 4-0</span><p>The Bruins beat Cal, San Diego State, Purdue and Maryland, scoring 54 in their last outing. They enter Oregon after a bye.</p><dl><dt>Latest result · idle October 3</dt><dd>2026-09-26 · W 54–3 away vs Maryland</dd><dt>AP movement</dt><dd>Up 2</dd><dt>Next game</dt><dd>2026-10-10 · away vs Oregon</dd></dl><details><summary>Unbeaten audition · analysis<